  "description": "<iframe src=\"\" style=\"background-image: url('https://deadface.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/2026/img/wayfinder/art_heist_the_forgery.jpg');background-size:cover;background-position:center center;background-origin:content-box;background-repeat:no-repeat;background-color:rgba(40, 40, 40,0);min-height:80px;height:130px;width:100%;padding:10px;border:none\" title=\"Thumbnail\"></iframe>\r\n<sup>Created By: <code>@syyntax</code></sup>\r\n\r\nThe Turla Museum recently welcomed back five paintings from its Cyber Impressionism collection following a loan to a neighboring gallery. But museum officials have received intelligence suggesting that DEADFACE infiltrated the gallery during the exhibition and secretly replaced one of the original paintings with a forgery.\r\n\r\nAll five paintings were scanned and entered into the museum's digital archive upon their return. Although the artwork appears authentic, investigators suspect that the forger left behind traces of their work in the digital records.\r\n\r\nThe museum has provided copies of all five images and needs your help identifying the compromised artwork.\r\n\r\nCan you determine which painting was forged and recover the flag left behind?\r\n\r\nSubmit the flag as `deadface{flag-text}`.\r\n\r\n[Download ZIP](https://deadface.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/2026/challenges/for/for11/CTF_Forgery_Paintings.zip)(9.35MB)<br>\r\n<sup>SHA256: `f4d4d1185b94639bfbcfadb81abbea667977760dd31834dfc52d4d65a846cb12`</sup>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
